// A simple mean whose window is weighted by the volume behind each bar, so the
// bars that actually traded set the level.
//
// Exercises: a window over two series at once, the division that has no answer
// when a window traded nothing at all, and a comparison against the unweighted
// mean of the same window, which the two agree on only when volume is flat.

version 1

study("Volume weighted average", overlay = true, precision = 4)

len = input(20, "Length", min = 1, max = 1000)

plot(vwma(close, len), "Weighted", aqua, width = 2)
plot(sma(close, len), "Unweighted", fade(silver, 50))
